    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29173" root="عشب" body-key="E">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَشِبَ المَوْضِعُ</span></b>  and 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَشِبَتِ الأَرْضُ</span></b> : see 4. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَشِبَ</span> said of bread, (Yaakoob, TA,) <i>It was,</i> or
<i>became, dry,</i> (Yaakoob, K, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عشب</span>,
[so in the TA, app. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَشُبَ</span>,] inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَشَابَةٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُشُوبَةٌ</span>, said of a man, <i>He became dry,</i> or <i>tough,
by reason of leanness.</i> (Yaakoob, TA.)

